    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The impact of the multi-fracture interaction due to cold fluid injection into a geothermal reservoir is investigated by using boundary integral equation method. The numerical results show that a thermal stress interaction can occur when the fracture spacing is much larger than that required by the temperature interaction. The increment of the thermal stresses due to the fracture interaction can increase the fracture aperture, which is favorable to enhance recovery efficiency of the geothermal energy. Therefore, an optimized fracture spacing may be chosen to increase fracture apertures meanwhile avoid temperature interaction.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Zhou, Xiaoxian, Aydin, Atilla and Ghassemi, Ahmad. (2009). Numerical Analysis of Impact of Fracture Interaction in Response to Cold Fluid Injection Into a Hot Geothermal Reservoir. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/nc487hv3358",
